//? Title: FlowNetS: explicit tensor optical-flow fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Two frames must reveal where each visible point moves,including regions with weak texture or occlusion. This example predicts input-pixel displacement with six encoder scales and learned flow decoding. Hand warps,unit conversions and masked losses precede published Middlebury targets,visible SGD/Adam and pair-only restored inference,with every held-out motion error shown.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/flownets.cpp`.

> The method

FlowNetS concatenates two jointly centered RGB frames,encodes six scales,
and decodes a flow pyramid with learned feature/flow transposes and skips.
Every internal field remains in input-image pixels/20. A valid-block GT
pyramid supervises all heads through smooth endpoint objectives;only the two
observed frames enter prediction. Fixed and fitted constant references make
the small experiment’s generalization limits inspectable.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/flownets_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/flownets_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/flownets_concept.tikz > build/flownets_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/flownets_concept.svg build/flownets_concept.dvi > build/flownets_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
