> Published Middlebury targets with related families isolated

This report replaces the old external archive with a reproducible custom
subset of the official public frame10/11 and flow10.flo files. Download
`other-color-twoframes.zip` and `other-gt-flow.zip` from Middlebury’s data
page into `build/cnn-datasets/optical_flow`. The pinned SHA256 values are
`dc7afbab15a7da40b52d633f825191bf693e227320bb624546ed9f2f8d668e50` and
`e967b729cc47a493b3226515e0172224e503f7b14a54f97660f8d5f745632ab9`.
From the repository root,run:

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("optical_flow", (cache / "optical_flow").string());
}
```
// result_begin:
// Validated32/8/24 published-GT crops with disjoint scene families.
// result_end

C++ validates little-endian PIEH ingress and image dimensions,then uses
tensor finite/abs<1e9 masks to zero unknown flow. Original RGB is divided by255;
**no image or flow resize** changes physical displacement units. On each
scene,a5x5 origin grid floors[0,.25,.5,.75,1]*(dimension-64). Take the first
eight row-major unique crops with>409 valid GT samples. This declared
validity-only rule never reads predictions or benchmark scores. The manifest
records every scene,family,source dimension and crop coordinate.

Fitting has Dimetrodon,Grove2,Grove3,Hydrangea(32 crops,three families).
Validation has RubberWhale(eight crops,one family). Test has Urban2,Urban3,
Venus(24 crops,two families). Related Grove and Urban scenes remain together.
Crops overlap within a scene;24 test crops are **three source pairs**,not24
independent sequences. The published data include photographed and rendered
scenes. These custom crops are not official benchmark evaluation.

A fixed zero field has no fitted parameters. For the constant reference,fit
two input-pixel coordinates by one explicit SGD(.5) update on the sum of
the two masked-coordinate MSEs. The independent closed-form mean only checks
the result. Save that fitted tensor for the later comparison.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flownets_prior.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";

  std::filesystem::path root = cache / "optical_flow";
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_FLOW_DIR"))
    root = p;
  else
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("optical_flow", root.string());
  const auto split = m::LoadFlowPairs(root);

  n::ParameterStore constant(173, n::DType::Float64);
  const auto q = constant.get("flow", {2}, n::init::zeros());
  n::OptimizerConfig opt;
  opt.kind = n::OptimizerKind::Sgd;
  n::Optimizer sgd(constant, .5, opt);
  const auto target = split.fit.flow.to(n::DType::Float64),
             mask = split.fit.valid.to(n::DType::Float64);
  for (int step = 0; step < 1; ++step) {
    const auto loss = n::sum(
        n::sum(mask * n::square(q.reshape({1, 1, 1, 2}) - target), {0, 1, 2}) / n::sum(mask));
    sgd.minimize(loss);
  }
  const auto fitted = q.detach().to(n::DType::Float32);
  const auto closed = m::FitMeanFlow(split.fit);
  const auto expected =
      n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{closed[0], closed[1]}, {2}).to(n::DType::Float32);
  const double parity = n::max(n::abs(fitted - expected)).item();
  if (parity > 1e-8)
    return 1;
  const auto first = m::FlowBatch(split.fit, {0, 8, 16, 24});
  const auto reference = n::ones(first.flow.shape()) * fitted.reshape({1, 1, 1, 2});
  const auto warped = m::FlowWarp(first.second, reference).value;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  n::save_npz("build/flownets_prior.npz", {{"flow", fitted}});
  n::save_image_grid(m::FlowPreviewTiles(first, reference, warped),
                     "figures/flownets_inputs.png", 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 2);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars({0., 1.}, fitted.to_vector<double>(), "SGD-fitted mean", {147, 51, 234})
      .title("Visible SGD fits constant input-pixel flow")
      .x_label("0 horizontal,1 vertical")
      .y_label("input-image pixels")
      .y_limits(-1.1, .35)
      .size(950, 480);
  plot.save_svg("build/flownets_prior.svg");
  std::print("One SGD(.5) update;mean oracle parity {:.3g};dx/dy {:.6f}/{:.6f}px.\n| split | "
             "crops | scenes | related families | GT pixels |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
             parity, fitted.to_vector<double>()[0], fitted.to_vector<double>()[1]);
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::string, m::FlowData>> splits = {
      {"fit", split.fit}, {"validation", split.validation}, {"test", split.test}};
  for (const auto &item : splits) {
    const auto scenes = item.second.scene_ids.to_vector<int>(),
               families = item.second.family_ids.to_vector<int>();
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", item.first, item.second.first.size(0),
               std::set<int>(scenes.begin(), scenes.end()).size(),
               std::set<int>(families.begin(), families.end()).size(),
               n::count_nonzero(item.second.valid).item<std::int64_t>());
  }
}
```
