// result_end
\caption(Forty-eight visible Adam updates with all five pyramid losses. Validation selects the checkpoint using only its held-out fitting-family complement;the test comparison remains separate.)
\alttext(Forty-eight visible Adam updates with all five pyramid losses. Validation selects the checkpoint using only its held-out fitting-family complement;the test comparison remains separate.)


\image(figures/flownets_metrics.svg)
\caption(Held-out equal-crop-weighted EPE compares trained,initial,zero and SGD-constant flow. The second panel separates the three source image pairs;overlapping crops are not independent sequences.)
\alttext(Held-out aggregate and source-pair endpoint errors,including simple fixed and fitted references.)

\image(figures/flownets_predictions.png)
\caption(All24 held-out crops,two six-panel tiles per row. Within each:frame1,frame2,published GT HSV,predicted HSV,EPE/5 in red,and backward-warped frame2. Order is eight Urban2,eight Urban3,eight Venus. Black warp borders denote incomplete source coverage;invalid GT colors/errors are black.)
\alttext(Actual Middlebury frame pairs and published motion targets compared with learned vectors,errors and image warps.)

The selected epoch1 model has test EPE4.246750px,compared with4.205583
for its initialization,3.916913 for zero flow and4.174930 for the fitted
constant. All42 leaves fit,but this run does not improve held-out motion
quality. Urban2/Urban3/Venus errors2.541693/4.478318/5.720239px also show
why a single aggregate hides substantial source-pair differences.

A lower short fitting objective need not improve motion estimates on new
scene families. The source pair counts,zero/constant references and actual
warps expose this distinction. There is no pretraining,FlyingChairs training,
online augmentation,or official benchmark claim. Published GT is used only
for supervision,declared support filtering and evaluation,not as an inference input.

> Conclusion

Tensor coordinate,unit,transpose,masked-loss and metric checks establish the optical-flow mechanism. Published targets and auditable family-disjoint crops then support visible optimization of a constant and every FlowNetS leaf. Pair-only restored inference is immutable;actual held-out fields and warps show the limits of the short fit.

> References

- [Fischer et al.(2015),FlowNet:Learning Optical Flow with Convolutional Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.06852).
- [NVIDIA FlowNetS architecture](https://github.com/NVIDIA/flownet2-pytorch/blob/master/networks/FlowNetS.py).
- [Middlebury public optical-flow data](https://vision.middlebury.edu/flow/data/).
- [Middlebury .flo format specification](https://vision.middlebury.edu/flow/code/flow-code/README.txt).
- [Baker et al.(2011),A Database and Evaluation Methodology for Optical Flow](https://vision.middlebury.edu/flow/floweval-ijcv2011.pdf).
